ODKI VBT — License Overview
============================

This repository is "open core": most of it is open source, the tracking
engine is source-available. There is no single license for the whole
repository; GitHub's automatic license detection will not describe it
correctly from this file. Every source file names its license in an
SPDX-License-Identifier line at the top. The licensor of everything
below that is not third-party is Lodovico Cortelazzo (ODKI).

Which file is under which license
---------------------------------

- Tracking engine — PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 with additional
  permissions, see LICENSE-ENGINE. Source-available, NOT open source.
    Firmware/VBT_Quaternions/MotionTracker.cpp, MotionTracker.h
    Firmware/tools/host_replay/replay.cpp, Firmware/tools/full_replay/harness.cpp
      (offline tools that compile the engine in)
    Firmware/DOCUMENTATION.md and the figures in Firmware/img/
  Free for personal, hobby and study use, for research for the benefit
  of public knowledge, and for universities, public research
  organisations, charities and the other organisations the license
  lists. Commercial use — including selling devices or kits that run the
  engine, or building it into a product — needs a commercial licence
  from ODKI (contact@odki.tech). Units from ODKI may be used for any
  purpose. The ideas and algorithm the documentation explains are not
  restricted; explaining them does not make them proprietary, and short
  quotations for study, criticism or review are free.

- Everything else in the firmware and the tools — Apache License 2.0,
  see LICENSE-APACHE and NOTICE. Open source.
    Firmware/VBT_Quaternions/ except the engine and src/Fusion/
      (VBT_Quaternions.ino, Config.h, TrackingTypes.h, BleServer,
      BatteryMonitor, PowerManager, StatusLED, FusionOrientation)
    Firmware/tools/ except the two files named above (log viewer, live
      monitor, host_replay and full_replay scripts, the regression and
      calibration tests, the validation pipeline and its PROTOCOL.md)
    Firmware/firmware-release/README.md, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md,
      TRADEMARKS.md and the other repository documents, unless they say
      otherwise

- BLE protocol specification — Firmware/BLE_PROTOCOL.md only (not the
  code that implements it): CC0 1.0, see the note at the top of that
  file. Anyone may build a client or a compatible device from it.

- Hardware design — Hardware/ (bill of materials, CAD files, assembly
  and bootloader instructions): CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, see LICENSE-HARDWARE.

- Third-party code — keeps its own license:
    Firmware/VBT_Quaternions/src/Fusion/ — x-io Fusion, MIT (its
      LICENSE.md in that folder)
  Firmware binaries (Firmware/firmware-release/*.zip and the firmware on
  units from ODKI) also contain libraries from the Arduino board package
  (among them the Arduino core for nRF52 under the GNU LGPL 2.1) — see
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

- Companion app — Apps/: the published builds (e.g. the Android APK)
  are proprietary software of Lodovico Cortelazzo (ODKI). No license is
  granted for them beyond installing and using them; see Apps/README.md.

Earlier versions
----------------

Firmware and tools up to and including v3.11.31 (main branch, commit
7c8d753) were released under the GNU GPL v3.0
modified by the Commons Clause License Condition v1.0. Copies received
under those terms stay under those terms; they do not apply to v3.12.0
and later.

Names and contributions
-----------------------

No license here grants the ODKI name or logo (TRADEMARKS.md).
Contributions to the official repository are covered by the Contributor
License Agreement in CONTRIBUTING.md.

See README.md for a plain-language summary.
